# Travel pages

Canonical workflow: [docs/travel-page-system.md](../../docs/travel-page-system.md) and skill `create-travel-page`.

## Hard rules

- Source of truth is `trip.yaml` beside the trip HTML. Regenerate HTML from yaml; do not treat hand-edited HTML as durable.
- Working photos live under `assets/images/Travel-Pages-Images/`. Year thumbs under `assets/images/gallary/` (spelling).
- Cover/hero source file must be named `COVER` / `Cover` (any image extension). Same source → two crops unless user overrides.
- Picture # badges stay visible on public pages.
- Prefer Chile leftover **reading flow** (text beside 1–2 leftovers, then full width). Use `assets/css/travel-trip.css` + generator.
- **NEVER** clear after only the first leftover paragraph. ALL section `<p>` tags must stay inside `.travel-leftover-wrap` **before** `clear:both`. The generator + `layout-guards` / `validate-trip` enforce this — do not hand-edit leftover HTML in a way that reintroduces the blank column beside tall photos.
- Run tooling via `cd travel-page-tool && npm run travel -- <command>`. Agent runs CLI; user reviews gates.
- Never auto-commit or push. Warn before staging huge `_incoming/` dumps (~prefer gitignore).
- Three gates: (1) photo order (2) story outline + crop previews + multipage ask (3) finished page QA.
- Do not mass-edit old trips. New trips use the generator.
- **No hyphens or dashes in trip prose** (no compound adjectives, em dashes, or en dashes). Rephrase in words. Keep hyphens only in proper names the user wrote and in file/slug paths.
